Description: OpenSSL 3 (that of the base system of FreeBSD 15) takes a TLS peer that closes the connection without close_notify for an attack on the end of the data: "SSL: ... unexpected eof while reading", a warning and a failed read in https://, ssl://, tls:// streams and SoapClient, where OpenSSL 1.1.1 gave the end of the data (bug #79589, GH-8369; many servers close so); SSL_OP_IGNORE_UNEXPECTED_EOF keeps the behaviour of OpenSSL 1.1.1, as PHP 8.1 and later do
Origin: php-src commit 74f75db0c3665677ec006cd379fd561feacffdc6 (Jakub Zelenka, 15.05.2022, PHP 8.1.7), as Ondřej Surý carries it for 5.6 (php5.6 5.6.40-105, debian/patches/0199-Fix-bug-79589-ssl3_read_n-unexpected-eof-while-readi.patch), without its whitespace changes; its test with the SKIPIF of 5.6 (an online test, skipped with SKIP_ONLINE_TESTS)

diff --git a/ext/openssl/tests/bug79589.phpt b/ext/openssl/tests/bug79589.phpt
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c778afdc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ext/openssl/tests/bug79589.phpt
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+--TEST--
+Bug #79589: TLS unexpected EOF failure
+--SKIPIF--
+<?php
+if (!extension_loaded("openssl")) die("skip openssl not loaded");
+if (getenv("SKIP_ONLINE_TESTS")) die("skip online test");
+?>
+--FILE--
+<?php
+
+$release = file_get_contents(
+    'https://chromedriver.storage.googleapis.com/LATEST_RELEASE',
+    false,
+    stream_context_create(['ssl' => ['verify_peer'=> false]])
+);
+echo gettype($release);
+
+?>
+--EXPECT--
+string
diff --git a/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c b/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
index ce7567a9..540543a6 100644
--- a/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
@@ -1528,6 +1528,11 @@ int php_openssl_setup_crypto(php_stream *stream,
 	ssl_ctx_options &= ~SSL_OP_DONT_INSERT_EMPTY_FRAGMENTS;
 #endif
 
+#ifdef SSL_OP_IGNORE_UNEXPECTED_EOF
+	/* Only for OpenSSL 3+ to keep OpenSSL 1.1.1 behavior */
+	ssl_ctx_options |= SSL_OP_IGNORE_UNEXPECTED_EOF;
+#endif
+
 #if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10000000L
 	if (!GET_VER_OPT("disable_compression") || zend_is_true(*val)) {
 		ssl_ctx_options |= SSL_OP_NO_COMPRESSION;
